e result:\n\\[\n542_{10} - 222_{10} = 320_{10}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Convert the result back to base 9\n\nTo convert \\(320_{10}\\) to base 9, we repeatedly divide by 9 and keep track of the remainders:\n\n\\[\n320 \\div 9 = 35 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5\n\\]\n\\[\n35 \\div 9 = 3 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 8\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\div 9 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 3\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get:\n\\[\n320_{10} = 385_9\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{385_9}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{385_9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:405"}
